From 8c83eb1a37933cfaabf08d0ef86f2ac688fbe4ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@example.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 19:00:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add real CBR/RAR and PDF support, plus an actual test suite

Format support:
- CBR/RAR: replace the fake support (fragile CDN fallback chain, broken
  dependency version) with node-unrar-js, which wraps the official unrar
  library compiled to WebAssembly. This genuinely decodes RAR archives --
  no more 'convert to CBZ' workaround required. Password-protected RAR is
  detected and rejected with a clear message.
- PDF: new format support via pdfjs-dist. Each page renders to canvas at
  2x scale and exports as a PNG blob URL, converging on the same
  {files, cache} shape CBZ/CBR already use, so ReaderPanel and the
  cover-thumbnail logic in TownScene stay format-agnostic.
- TownScene: file input now accepts .pdf, upload regex extended, and the
  old RAR-specific 'not supported' dialog is replaced with a generic
  decode-error dialog (RAR failures are now genuine decode errors --
  corrupt file, password-protected, etc. -- not 'unsupported format').

Testing:
- Added Vitest for unit tests: color/HSL math, dominant-color extraction
  (via a hand-built fake canvas, no DOM needed), and plot placement math
  (extracted computeSlotPosition into a standalone pure function
  specifically so it's testable without constructing a full WebGL scene).
- New Playwright e2e specs: tests/cbz.spec.js (real upload + corrupt-file
  error handling), tests/pdf.spec.js (same, using pdf-lib to generate a
  genuinely valid test PDF). tests/cbr.spec.js rewritten -- it can only
  test the error-handling path, since no open-source RAR encoder exists
  to generate a real archive fixture; this limitation is documented
  in-file and in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md and docs/QA_CHECKLIST.md rather
  than papered over.
- tests/ui.spec.js: added a regression test asserting the canvas fills
  the viewport, guarding against the tiny-canvas-in-the-corner bug
  recurring silently.
- docs/QA_CHECKLIST.md: new manual QA checklist covering what automated
  tests can't (real RAR files, real-device testing, subjective visual
  checks).

Docs updated (ARCHITECTURE.md, ROADMAP.md, USAGE.md) to reflect all of
the above honestly, including the known limitation that all three
formats currently decode eagerly rather than lazily.
